infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two boundaries, two fixes
  desc context.bind keeps context across in-process callbacks; inject/extract carries the trace-id across a process boundary
  compares
    - label context.bind / .with (in-process)
      children
        - label Same process memory
          desc Captures and restores the OTel context within one process
        - label Fixes setTimeout, setImmediate, queueMicrotask
          desc And callbacks passed to third-party libraries
        - label Restores trace-id when the callback fires
          desc Deferred work links to the request's span
        - label Writes nothing to the wire
          desc No traceparent in any outbound message
    - label inject / extract (cross-process)
      children
        - label Crosses a process boundary
          desc Producer and consumer share no memory
        - label Fixes Kafka, RabbitMQ, SQS, Pub/Sub
          desc Producer injects, consumer extracts
        - label Writes trace-id into the message wire format
          desc traceparent and baggage written into headers
        - label context.bind alone is not enough
          desc Only injecting into headers carries the trace-id across
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
